  "findings": [
    "COMPAS shows a false-positive-rate gap of +0.143 (African-American minus Caucasian): African-American defendants are incorrectly labeled high-risk at a higher rate than Caucasian defendants.",
    "Counterfactual debiasing (Model B) reduces the FPR gap from +0.163 to +0.143. However, the gap does not reach zero because race correlates with other features (proxy bias).",
    "Among all mitigation methods, 'ExponentiatedGradient (EqualizedOdds)' achieves the lowest equalized-odds difference (0.0546) at accuracy 0.6534. Best trade-off does not necessarily mean perfect fairness \u2014 examine FPR and FNR gaps separately.",
    "Fairness-accuracy trade-off: the best mitigation method reduces equalized-odds difference by 0.2654 at a cost of 0.0158 accuracy points (1.58%). This trade-off is inherent and cannot be eliminated.",
    "Limitations: race and sex are binary here due to COMPAS data constraints. Counterfactual debiasing cannot eliminate proxy bias through correlated legal-merit features. These results apply to Broward County, FL (2013-2014) only and should not be extrapolated to other jurisdictions or time periods."
